# BUGS

The controllers have no count of a line's users: two devices that share a line (one `RSTL` index in two devices' tables) each hold or release it for both, and the last command wins.
A line's name isn't known to the driver, only its index, so `status` shows an index and a state.
The driver has not run on the board: the index map is the hardware's as its tables give it, checked against no board but through the GPU's and the display engines' lines when mali(3) and linlon(3) use it.
There is no read of a line that no command has named.
